  "transcript": "User: Hello — I got your flyer about after-hours calls. We miss calls when we're out on jobs.\nAgent: Got it, thanks for calling in and for mentioning the flyer.  \n\nSo when a call comes in and you’re out on a job, what usually happens to that call — does it ring through to you, go to voicemail, or just ring out?\nUser: It usually goes to voicemail if we're out on a job.\nAgent: Yeah, that makes sense — a lot of folks rely on voicemail by default.  \n\nWhen those calls hit voicemail, do people usually leave a message, or do you notice they tend to just hang up and call the next company?\nUser: Most hang up, but about 8 missed calls go to voicemail each week.\nAgent: Gotcha, so most people just bail and a handful actually leave a message.  \n\nWhen those calls don’t get picked up live and they hang up, how does that impact you — do you feel like you’re losing real jobs to competitors because of it?\nUser: Yes, I believe about 50% would book with us if someone answered their call live.\nAgent: Makes sense, and thanks for being that specific — that helps a ton.  \n\nHas anyone ever walked you through what those missed calls are actually costing you each month, or has it mostly just been a feeling that you’re losing jobs?\nUser: It's mostly a feeling, but with an average job value of about $2,500, I suspect it's significant.\nAgent: You’re not wrong — on your numbers, those missed calls are adding up to around $43,000 a month in jobs that could be slipping away.  \n\nSo… to actually plug that leak, I’d like to walk you through how we can turn those after-hours and on-the-job missed calls into booked work — would you be open to a quick 20‑minute call with us this week to see it on your numbers?\nUser: Yes, I'm open to a call this week to see how it works.\nAgent: Nice, that makes a lot of sense.  \n\nFirst thing so we can line that up properly — what’s your first name?\nUser: I'm Susan. I own Cornerstone Remodeling here in Denver.\nAgent: Nice to meet you, Susan — and Cornerstone’s a great name by the way.  \n\nAnd just to make sure I’ve got everything right, Susan… what’s your last name?\nUser: I prefer to keep it informal, but I’m the owner of Cornerstone Remodeling.\nAgent: Got it, totally fine to keep it informal, Susan.  \n\nQuick check on your contact info — the number you’re calling from now, is that the best one to text your appointment confirmation to?\nUser: No, the best contact number is +13039150001.\nAgent: Mhm, perfect — I’ve got that number down.  \n\nSo for this demo, would you rather do it later today or sometime tomorrow?\nUser: I’d prefer sometime tomorrow, if possible.\nAgent: Got it, tomorrow works.  \n\nI can get you in as soon as Wednesday at 4:45 pm or 5:30 pm Mountain time — which of those works better for you?\nUser: Yes, book it for Wednesday at 4:45 pm Mountain time.\nAgent: One moment while I confirm that.\nAgent: Thanks, Susan! You’re all set for Wednesday at 4:45 pm Mountain time. You’ll get a text in a moment with the confirmation — you can tap to add it to your calendar or reschedule if something comes up. Is there anything else I can help you with right now?",
